  "findings": [
    "Bounded support: fresh plain depth4, mixed-size/bold depth and direction, consumed-empty root/children, and mixed-size/subscript baselines pass. Fresh WBS membership is5/9 after versus1/9 before, with no lost pass. Measured main height replaces BOX_H in the pre-existing subtree/attachment equations. Default Padding10 and font12 are corroborated by pinned plantuml.skin; no unexplained new geometry constant found.",
    "Counterexamples wbs_multiline_root, wbs_multiline_child and wbs_newline_empty remain whole-output failures. WBSDiagram.addIdea calls Display.getWithNewlines before FtileBoxOld creates a SheetBlock. SheetBlock1.initMap stacks stripe heights and takes the maximum stripe width. Rust parse_wbs stores literal backslash-n in WbsNode.label, and wbs::measure/emit_box send the whole label through single-line APIs. Root multiline canvas is Java152x163 versus Rust152x149; multiline child Java205x221 versus Rust231x207; leading/interior/trailing blank lines Java94x205 versus Rust139x149. The correction improves styled dimensions but does not supply a display-level multiline model.",
    "Counterexample wbs_boxless: Java CommandWBSItemOld captures the underscore as SHAPE, IdeaShape.fromDesc selects the non-box branch of WBSTextBlock.buildMain, and text gets margins0,3,1,1. Rust WbsNode has no shape field, parse_wbs leaves underscore inside the label, and emit_box always paints a padded rectangle. Java181x187 versus Rust222x205. This is an existing parser/model/consumer dependency, not permission to compensate coordinates or introduce a feature in this review.",
    "WBS repair is supported for tested single-line box labels only. Four valid shape/multiline counterexamples reject the whole claimed result under the unchanged acceptance rule; no scope waiver or combined sibling correctness is asserted."
  ],
